Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='androidportal', at=datetime(2026, 9, 4, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The Android app is a portal: a WebView onto the box, https only, no credential, native only for OS integration', body='*The Android app is a PORTAL* (`android/`, 2026-09-04): a WebView onto `https://<your-box>.<tailnet>.ts.net/`, the box its APK PROFILE names (`nix/apk-profile.nix`, 2026-10-23, `docs/APKPROFILE-PLAN-2026-10-23.md`) or, for the generic APK, the one typed at first launch and kept once that box answers `GET /api/portal` with its Firebase sender (443 since 2026-09-05), https ONLY: cleartext is refused for every host, an SSL or load error is the offline screen and never a downgrade (2026-10-09), and data extraction rules keep everything out of backup and device transfer; screenshots stay allowed (the owner sends them). No fold, fulfillment, verifier or HTML in Java: `MainActivity.java` keeps this origin in the WebView, sends other links to the system browser, never proceeds past an SSL error, and draws its failure screen with Android widgets. NO credential: `tailscale whois` sees the phone\'s login, so removing the device from the tailnet removes the app. Native is earned only by OS integration (deep links, push, share target, widget), each a shell over the same API; details in ARCHITECTURE §11.2. The rules: links are ordinary https URLs the site vouches for (`web/static/.well-known/assetlinks.json`); push is a DATA message the app composes, never an FCM "notification", with no Firebase SDK; the widget prints the number as the box printed it; the APK is an unsigned build signed outside (`scripts/sign-apk.sh`, `$SUZATARY_KEYSTORE`), and every update MUST use the same signing key (losing the keystore costs a reinstall everywhere).', rationale='Decided 2026-09-04; port 443 since 2026-09-05; https only since 2026-10-09; the APK profile since 2026-10-23 (docs/APKPROFILE-PLAN-2026-10-23.md).', supersedes=()))